  "description": "TMF Business Process Framework knowledge graph with correct relationships. Accurate process hierarchies, proper department assignments, and complete workflow connections based on TMF eTOM Framework dataset.",
  "question": "How does the TMF eTOM framework organize customer-facing operations processes, and what is the workflow from order handling through service activation to billing?",
  "llm_response": "The TMF eTOM framework organizes customer-facing operations through the FAB (Fulfillment, Assurance, Billing) horizontal process flow. When a customer places an order, Order Handling in CRM captures the request and validates it against product catalog offerings. This triggers Service Configuration & Activation in Service Management, which orchestrates the technical service setup. Service activation then triggers Resource Provisioning in Resource Management to allocate network resources. Once services are active, Billing & Revenue Management captures usage data through Rating & Discounting, generates invoices via Bill Invoice Management, and manages collections. Throughout this process, Assurance processes (Problem Handling, Service Quality Management) monitor service performance and handle issues. All these processes are governed by Product Lifecycle Management which defines the offerings, and Enterprise Management which provides financial and strategic oversight.",
